      "calculationScope": "EXACT_MANUAL_CALCULATION",
      "manualArithmetic": "Volume, charge and energy per second yield m³/s,A,W respectively despite sharing a time denominator. Integrating a normal velocity profile over the section gives Qv=S*vbar, where vbar is the area mean normal velocity; uniform normal intensity gives receivedP=I*S. Mass collection converts tovolume only through density. Reviewer6units/3s gives2 in each appropriate dimension; area2m²*3m/s gives6m³/s, while2m²*3W/m² gives6W. Conservation is incoming-minus-outgoing equals accumulation. Tank3in/2out stores1m³/s; a chosen charge-storing boundary3Ain/2Aout stores1C/s. Include capacitor branch current to retain Kirchhoff balance rather than declaring KCL invalid. Different densities can preserve massflow without equal volumeflow, outside the incompressible premise.",
      "manualFeasibility": "PASS_AI_EXACT",
      "physicalAssumptions": "Incompressible liquid and cross-sectional area-mean normal velocity for Qv=S*vbar. Uniform normal beam and small receiving area forP=I*S. Volume/mass distinctions requiredensity. Steady boundary with no relevant accumulation for equal incoming/outgoing sums; include all branches or storage terms in a transient. Source is a sufficient steady model, not a claim KCL stops applying to a complete circuit with capacitors.",
      "pedagogicalReview": "Shared area/time structure is contrasted with distinct transported quantities anddimensions. Chosen arrows support signed balance and explicit storage checks; doesnotidentifycharge/currentwithenergy/power.",
